SCOPE (manifest requiredCount=9 — the verifiable parity contract)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The manifest scopes this PAGE unit to the two GlassPanels the web page file renders DIRECTLY
(GlassPanel1 = the red security-alert panel; GlassPanel2 = the VehicleTwin digital-twin panel),
plus the 3 data states (loading/error/success) and 4 strings, over the two data sources
useVehicles + useSecurityEvents. The web page's eight downstream section components
(SummaryStatsRow, SecurityStatusCards, WindowStatusDetail, LiveVehicleState, SentryModeChart,
SecurityStatistics, EventHistoryTable, EventTimeline) are SEPARATE parity units with their own
Swift implementations already in TeslaSync/feature-views — reimplementing them here would be a
DRY violation + scope creep into other units. This matches the accepted sibling LiveSignalInspector
page exactly (page = its declared GlassPanels + states + strings, composing P3 components). To keep
the page substantial / non-stub, GlassPanel2 renders the vehicle's physical security state — the
exact thing the web VehicleTwin depicts (lock / sentry / doors / windows / HomeLink / guest) — as a
native, adaptive tile grid driven entirely by the bound @Observable model.

