DISPOSITION
================================================================================
A complete, HIG-native SwiftUI SecurityAccessPage shipped at parity with the web source: a pure @Observable state
holder (ADR-004 — no networking in the view) that owns the vehicles source state (web useVehicles) and the per-vehicle
security feed (web useSecurityEvents + /security/latest), deriving isSecure/sentry-uptime/last-lock-change through
SecurityAccessLogic (ported faithfully from the web helpers.ts). The two web GlassPanels — the security-alert panel
(shown when not secure) and the digital-twin panel (the vehicle's physical lock/sentry/door/window/HomeLink/guest
state) — are rendered with the P2 tokens + P3 shared components (TSGlassPanel/TSAlertBanner/TSEmptyState/TSSpinner/
TSButton/TSPageTitle/TSPanelTitle/TSStatusBadge) — no hand-rolled glass; every visible string from
Localizable.xcstrings with the web key names; adaptive across macOS/iPad/iPhone via the twin's LazyVGrid; deep-linkable
via the new .securityAccess route (AppRouteParser resolves /security-access). Verified on BOTH idioms by isolated
Swift 6 strict-concurrency type-checks (0/0) and an executed model harness (34/34), with the Shared.xcframework built
GREEN. The full xcodebuild scheme is RED ONLY due to TWO pre-existing, out-of-scope sibling errors
(Input.Previews.swift:88/:101, #Preview return-in-ViewBuilder), with ZERO diagnostics in any of my files.

